FINAL ANSWER:
## Short answer

- **`lib/grape_entity/exposure`:** most of the knowledge sits with Vladimir Kochnev, but they last committed on 2015-09-18. The practical reviewer is **Marco Silva**, with a caveat about their two email addresses (explained below).
- **Delegator code:** Vladimir Kochnev again. Nobody who has written delegator code is still active, so there's no one to route reviews to with confidence.
- **Most commits vs. most code:** no. dblock has the most commits, but Vladimir Kochnev owns the most surviving code.

All figures come from surviving-lines (`git blame -w -M -C`) at HEAD 0217c80, with activity measured as of 2026-10-05. "Active" means at least one commit in the 365 days before that date.

## `lib/grape_entity/exposure` (609 non-blank lines, 732 counting blank lines)

| Author | Non-blank lines | Counting blank lines | Last commit here | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Vladimir Kochnev | 331 (54.4%) | 400 (54.6%) | 2015-09-18 | inactive |
| Marco Silva | 117 (19.2%) | 143 (19.5%) | 2026-08-03 | active |
| Alexander Yunin | 55 (9.0%) | 61 (8.3%) | 2016-07-04 | inactive |
| James McCarthy | 48 (7.9%) | 58 (7.9%) | 2017-04-05 | inactive |

- **Vladimir Kochnev** owns `base.rb`, `nesting_exposure.rb`, `nested_exposures.rb` and `represent_exposure.rb`, plus the formatter and block exposures, which nobody else has written.
- **Marco Silva** wrote 100% of `grouped_exposure.rb`.
- **The caveat:** those 117 lines are under `<email redacted>`, which the tool flags as a placeholder address it can't tie to a person. It strongly suggests (from name and address only) that this is the same person as `marco.silva@kestrel.example`, who has 23 more lines and is active. If you confirm that, Marco is the best active reviewer; it's a guess until then.
- **Weak fallback:** Anna Kowalczyk is the only other active author, with 4 lines (0.7%).
- **Concentration:** bus factor is 1 (the fewest authors who together hold 50% of the lines). 9 files, 80.8% of the lines, are orphaned: their top owner is inactive and no active person holds 20% or more.

## Delegator code (`delegator.rb`, `delegators/`, `exposure/delegator_exposure.rb`)

Together these are 97 non-blank lines, 109 counting blank lines.

| Author | Non-blank lines | Counting blank lines | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Vladimir Kochnev | 69 (71.1%) | 73 (67.0%) | inactive |
| Paul Padier | 11 (11.3%) | 12 (11.0%) | inactive, last commit 2021 |
| James McCarthy | 6 (6.2%) | 12 (11.0%) | inactive |
| Marco Silva | 4 (4.1%) | 4 (3.7%) | active, last commit here 2026-07-21 |

- All 6 files are orphaned, and the bus factor is 1.
- In `delegators/`, nobody with lines there is active. All 61 lines were moved there from the old `lib/grape_entity/delegator/` directory; the credit stays with the people who wrote them, not whoever moved them.
- Marco Silva is the only active author, so they're the only person you can route to. With 4 lines, though, they're a reviewer by default rather than an expert.

## Who has effectively left

Only 7 of 87 authors committed in the last year, and they hold 10.7% of the non-blank lines. The remaining 89.3% belong to people with no commit in that window. The biggest owners who have gone quiet:

- **Vladimir Kochnev:** 1,010 lines (18.7%) / 1,180 with blank lines (17.6%); last commit 2015-09-18.
- **Mark Madsen:** 731 (13.5%) / 921 (13.7%); last commit 2013-01-20.
- **dblock:** 565 (10.4%) / 725 (10.8%); last commit 2016-11-20.
- **peter scholz:** 427 (7.9%) / 586 (8.7%); last commit 2024-04-10.
- **Alexander Yunin, James McCarthy, Dmitry Tsepelev and Paul Padier** are also inactive.

Counted only on the lines of active people, the bus factor is 2 (Marc Rohloff and Andrei Subbota). Neither has meaningful lines in the exposure or delegator code.

## Most commits vs. most code

- **dblock** has the most commits: 52 (18.2%). That figure already includes their four name variants under `<email redacted>`.
- **Vladimir Kochnev** has the most surviving lines: 1,010 non-blank (18.7%), 1,180 counting blank lines (17.6%), from only 11 commits (3.8%).
- **Mark Madsen** is second on lines (13.5%) with just 8 commits.

Repo-wide, the bus factor is 4 on both bases (16 authors to reach 80% of non-blank lines, 15 counting blank lines).

## What the numbers leave out

- **Copyright header commit:** b26feca by Lena Brandt was set aside because it's boilerplate.
- **Excluded files and bots:** `.rubocop_todo.yml` (generated) and dependabot's 5 lines aren't counted.
- **History start:** the history begins with an import on 2013-01-12. Older code is credited to whoever imported it.
- **Lines aren't understanding:** these figures show whose code is still there, not who understands it.

If you confirm the two Marco Silva addresses are the same person, I can add that line to `.mailmap`. I haven't written anything.

